    .map(n -&gt; n * 2)
    .collect(Collectors.toList());
System.out.println("Doubled: " + doubled);  // [10, 18, 16, 16, 2]

// Reduce (sum)
int sum = numbers.stream()
    .reduce(0, (a, b) -&gt; a + b);
System.out.println("Sum: " + sum);  // 31
Answer: The stream pipeline filters numbers greater than 5, removes duplicates, sorts them, takes the first element, and prints it. The original list remains unchanged. Output: 8.



